            <div xml:id="d44-a1">

                <pb facs="0158" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg50"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 11—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Senhor d’Mave to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I communicated to the minister of the foreign office the two letters in which
                    Messrs. Frank Norton and Levering &amp; Co. address themselves to the
                    consul-general of the United States in order to obtain the necessary permission
                    to deliver and accept telegrams in ordinary language. His excellency answered
                    that he regrets much but that for the present it will not be possible for the
                    Government to grant the request.</p>
                <p>Returning to Mr. Thompson the above-mentioned letters, I have the honor to renew
                    the assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. F. d’Mave.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
